# Callisto — root environment, read by docker-compose.yml and podman-compose.yml
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# This file is *only* for the container stacks. Compose reads it from the
# project root to interpolate ${...} in the compose files; it is not loaded by
# `npm run dev`, and neither app reads it at runtime.
#
# Both stacks share it. Compose looks for `.env` beside the compose file, not
# for a name matching the -f argument, so docker-compose.yml and
# podman-compose.yml read these same values. That is harmless — the two stacks
# bind the same ports and never run at once — but if you ever do need them to
# differ, pass `--env-file <path>` rather than renaming this file.
#
# Per-app configuration lives elsewhere and is injected with `env_file:`:
#
#   apps/server/.env   GEMINI_API_KEY, PORT, CORS_ORIGIN, the system prompt, …
#   apps/web/.env      PORT, and the same two NEXT_PUBLIC_* values below
#
# ── Why these two are duplicated ─────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are inlined into the browser bundle when Next builds, so
# they must be present as *build args* — which is what this file supplies. The
# copies in apps/web/.env drive `npm run dev`, where the build happens on the
# fly; in a container build they arrive too late to affect the bundle.
#
# Practical consequence: changing either value below requires a rebuild
# (`--build`), not a restart. Keep them in step with apps/web/.env, or the dev
# server and the container will point the browser at different backends.

# ── Where the browser reaches @callisto/server ───────────────────────────────
#
# These are resolved by the *visitor's* browser, not from inside the container,
# so loopback only works when the browser is on the same machine. Behind a
# reverse proxy on a public domain they must be the public URLs — the defaults
# below would make every visitor dial their own machine and fail to connect.
#
# Local containers (matches the compose defaults):
NEXT_PUBLIC_WS_URL=ws://127.0.0.1:3013/ws/session
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3013

# Behind nginx on a public domain, use the TLS scheme and your own host — and
# set CORS_ORIGIN in apps/server/.env to the matching https:// origin, or the
# WebSocket upgrade is rejected before a session opens. See
# docs/core/deployment.md.
#
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_WS_URL=wss://callisto.example.com/ws/session
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://callisto.example.com
